      "text": "laid hold on Jesus led him away to Caiaphas, Matt. 26:57. bound him … delivered him to Pontius Pilate, Matt. 27:2. when he was accused … he answered nothing, Matt. 27:12. they all condemned him to be guilty of death, Mark 14:64. Pilate asked him, Art thou the King of the Jews, Mark 15:2. clothed him with purple, and plaited a crown of thorns, Mark 15:17. shall be delivered unto the Gentiles, and … mocked, Luke 18:32. men that held Jesus mocked him, and smote him, Luke 22:63. Art thou the Christ? tell us, Luke 22:67. they said, What need we any further witness, Luke 22:71. said Pilate … I find no fault in this man, Luke 23:4. they cried, saying, Crucify him, Luke 23:21 (John 19:15). expedient … one man should die for the people, John 11:50. led him away to Annas first, John 18:13. high priest then asked Jesus of his disciples, John 18:19. Pilate … said, What accusation bring ye, John 18:29. when he was reviled, reviled not again, 1 Pet. 2:23.",
